WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.474
This slide focuses on Readable code starts with
names Start with the meaning of the

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:11.853
idea then connect it to the example and the larger
analytical workflow Names

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.606
should describe the role of a value This makes code
easier for future readers including

00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:23.756
you Use descriptive names Before running the example

00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:29.640
predict the output Run it in the browser inspect the
result then modify one input

00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:35.719
expression or value and run it again Notice whether
the shorter technique improves clarity

00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:37.719
or only makes the code harder to read
